PGP and GPG
PGP means Pretty Good Privacy - implements encryption for encrypting files, performing digital signing, and more. 
GPG is used in email to protect the confidentiality of emails

gpg --full-gen-key is the commands used to generate keys

gpg (or GnuPG) is an opensource implementation of PGP

Once you generate your key pair, you can share the public key with your contacts and decrypt what they send you with your private key. It's worth keeping a secure copy of the private key elsewhere, since if it's lost, all messages are also lost.
use gpg --import backup.key to import the backup key

To decrypt the messages, use this command:
gpg --decrypt confidential_message.gpg